collision of routes using different ?api-version

I was trying to see if I could map Azure APIs to Rocket routes. The `api-version` is a required parameter on almost all routes. Unfortunately, I get this error:

```
Error: Rocket failed to launch due to the following route collisions:
   >> (private_clouds_list) GET /subscriptions/<subscription>/providers/Microsoft.AVS/privateClouds?api-version=2021-06-01 collides with (private_clouds_list) GET /subscriptions/<subscription>/providers/Microsoft.AVS/privateClouds?api-version=2021-12-01
   >> Note: Route collisions can usually be resolved by ranking routes.
```

With this test:
``` rs
#[macro_use] extern crate rocket;

mod v2021_06_01 {
    #[get("/subscriptions/<subscription>/providers/Microsoft.AVS/privateClouds?api-version=2021-06-01")]
    pub fn private_clouds_list(subscription: &str) -> String {
        format!("v2021_06_01 private_clouds_list subscription {}", subscription)
    }
}

mod v2021_12_01 {
    #[get("/subscriptions/<subscription>/providers/Microsoft.AVS/privateClouds?api-version=2021-12-01")]
    pub fn private_clouds_list(subscription: &str) -> String {
        format!("v2021_12_01 private_clouds_list subscription {}", subscription)
    }
}

#[launch]
fn rocket() -> _ {
    rocket::build()
        .mount("/", routes![
            v2021_06_01::private_clouds_list,
            v2021_12_01::private_clouds_list,
        ])
}
```

I'm using the latest `master` commit abf996b026b601abb193d2f2081887b1de5e6ced.

I think using an `api-version` query param is many APIs is pretty common.

