Issue title: How can I provide a Stream API for quinn::RecvStream and datagram?

[TARGET]
You can convert a future which borrows a `Connection` into an owned future by moving it into an `async` block that owns a clone of the connection:

```rs
{
    let conn = this.conn.clone();
    async move { conn.read_datagram().await }
}
```

You'll need to replace this every time it completes, of course.

Alternatively, you could use something like [`futures::stream::unfold`](https://docs.rs/futures/latest/futures/stream/fn.unfold.html):

```rs
unfold(this.conn.clone(), |conn| async {
    let datagram = conn.read_datagram().await;
    Some((datagram, conn))
})
```

