Issue title: Supporting Marginalia (Queries Commenting Their Source)

[TARGET]
Yeah agreed on the on the custom logger having a use for `std::panic::Location`.

I like that API for the most part, but I'm thinking we should combine `append` to `prepend` to a single method otherwise there might be some confusion in edgecases (e.g.) what happens if I call:

```rust
builder.append().prepend().append()
```

This is a very ridiculous example (and would probably never happen, even spread across libraries as builders), but still no reason to introduce it I think!

So realistically I think having:

```rust
pub struct QueryMarginalia {
    // ...
}

impl QueryMarginalia {
    pub fn builder() -> QueryMarginaliaBuilder;
}

impl QueryMarginaliaBuilder {
    /// defaults to false
    pub fn should_prepend(&mut self, prepend: bool) -> &mut Self;

    /// Add a key/value pair to all marginalia entries.
    pub fn add(&mut self, key: impl Display, value: impl Display) -> &mut Self;

    pub fn add_caller_info(&mut self) -> &mut Self;

    // Where `Query` has the SQL string, the marginalia entries, and the caller location
    pub fn format(&mut self, format: impl Fn(Query, &mut Formatter) -> fmt::Result) -> &mut Self;
}

impl Into<QueryMarginalia> for &mut QueryMarginaliaBuilder { ... }
impl Into<QueryMarginalia> for QueryMarginaliaBuilder { ... }

impl PgConnectOptions {
    pub fn query_marginalia(&mut self, query_marginalia: impl Into<QueryMarginalia>) -> &mut Self;
}
```

> What do you think would be a more appropriate format? Passing file, line, and column as separate keys?

Yeah ideally those are all separate keys (As that's what existing tools do -- I'm not super tied to this, but probably a good idea to match)

